  "term": "early-onset Alzheimer’s disease",
  "definition": "Early-onset Alzheimer’s disease is Alzheimer’s disease beginning before age 65. In this source, it is described as having a different clinical profile from later-onset Alzheimer’s disease, with more widespread disruption of functional brain organization.",
